WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.070
- [Instructor] Can't sign
in to your Microsoft account

2
00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.540
or reset your password?

3
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.900
If you haven't set up
two-step verification,

4
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.160
here's how you can recover it.

5
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.413
Go to aka.ms/accountrecovery.

6
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:16.127
Enter the account you want to recover.

7
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.640
Note, if you haven't
signed into your account

8
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.480
in more than a year, the
emails and files tied

9
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.070
to that account cannot be recovered.

10
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.713
Inactive accounts expire
after after two years.

11
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.313
Enter an email address you have access to.

12
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.683
Then enter the CAPTCHA.

13
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.173
Select Next.

14
00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.533
We'll send a code to
the email you provided.

15
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.573
Enter the code and select Verify.

16
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:52.143
Then, enter your information
to help verify you're you.

17
00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:58.500
A few tips to get you
back into your account.

18
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.310
One, collect information
about your account

19
00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:02.690
before you start.

20
00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.390
This means things like contacts

21
00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:08.120
and exact subject lines for
Outlook or Hotmail accounts,

22
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.550
your console hardware
ID for Xbox accounts,

23
00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:15.453
or your SkypeID and names of
contacts for Skype accounts.

24
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.690
Two, think about when you created
or last used your account.

25
00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.340
Your information will likely reflect that.

26
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:26.230
Three, answer these questions
from a familiar device

27
00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.650
and location,

28
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.460
and four, enter as much
information as you can.

29
00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.810
It's okay to guess.

30
00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.733
Wrong answers won't count against you.

31
00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:39.403
After you've answered them, select Next.

32
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.200
Your information has been submitted.

33
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.733
We will typically respond within 24 hours.

34
00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:50.963
If approved, you'll get a
link to reset your password.

35
00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.660
If your request isn't approved,

36
00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.143
we'll let you know by email.

37
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.010
You can try to recover
your account again up

38
00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.970
to two times each day.

39
00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.200
You might remember something

40
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.893
that can help verify who you are.

41
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.030
Note, to ensure your account's security,

42
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.410
Microsoft can't help access

43
00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.520
or help you recover your account,

44
00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.310
but until you get back in,

45
00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.880
nobody else can access
your account either.

46
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.580
Your information will stay secure.

47
00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.000
If you ultimately cannot
recover your account,

48
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.523
you can create a new one
at account.microsoft.com.

49
00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:29.480
Need more help?

50
00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.393
Go to support.microsoft.com/account.
